-- title:
--   Summing an unused final transition gives the weighted prefix law
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega$ be a finite type with decidable equality and $P$ a Markov transition matrix on $\Omega$. For a list $\mathbf x=(x_1,\ldots,x_m)$, write $H_P(x;\mathbf x)=P(x,x_1)\cdots P(x_{m-1},x_m)$, with $H_P(x;[])=1$. Let $\mathbf x$ be any finite state list of length $N$ and $w:\Omega\to\mathbb R$ any real-valued initial weight. Then $$\sum_{\substack{z\in\Omega^{N+1}\\(z_0,\ldots,z_{N-1})=\mathbf x}}w(z_0)\prod_{i=0}^{N-1}P(z_i,z_{i+1})=\begin{cases}\sum_xw(x),&\mathbf x=[],\\ w(a)H_P(a;\mathbf y),&\mathbf x=a::\mathbf y.\end{cases}$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/StoppedRecordedTraceSubkernel.lean#L29-L71

